  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA PCA improves substantially with multiprofile avgpool (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1) compared with singleprofile and transformer aggregation, but there is still no evidence about whether image features contribute. config_011 tests an image-only ResNet50 model under the same multiprofile avgpool setting, isolating whether the image modality and the current profile/aggregation choice carry useful signal before adding fusion. This is the best next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about a core design decision with a simple standard baseline, avoids changing multiple variables by not jumping directly to multimodal fusion, and will inform whether future experiments should focus on improving the RNA representation or pursuing multimodal combinations."
